{
  "id": "ss.enemy.matriarch",
  "name": "Matriarch",
  "description": "The hive itself, arriving. Almost all of her is the brood chamber — one round translucent mass with the next wave already drifting inside it and a crown of spines standing off the shell, dragged by an amber head barely big enough to steer, drawn behind the body because it is not what is in charge. Round where the Courser is a dart, and the only body on the roster whose inside is the thing you look at: the pink is the brood, and it is the only pink here that is not an organ. She carries the largest organ anyway, because she is what all the others were announcing.\n\nThe chamber is built rather than drawn: six carapace plates around a ring of membrane, so every gap between them is pressure showing rather than a hole — the argument the Foundress makes along a gaster, made here around a circle. The crown is twelve separate spines at uneven lengths, not one star: a ring of even points is a cog, and a cog cannot flex when the body under it does. The seven eggs are seven parts for the same reason — the claim this body makes is that you are looking at its inside, and a seeded scatter is one egg stamped seven times.\n\nThe chamber breathes as one thing: its swell is a scale the whole rig is placed off, so spines, plates, seams, sac, rim and organ grow with it and nothing rides rigid on a body expanding under it; the breath travels the crown rather than arriving on every spine at once; the eggs drift inside on their own orbits; the legs are two links and take the weight late; the head nods and the maw works. `command` is her calling the brood in — not a windup, because she never attacks: the chamber draws in hard, lets go, and the release travels the ring the way the ring the game draws travels the floor. `lay` is one clutch leaving through the seam at the bottom, with the rest of the brood settling into the room it made. Drawn facing +x, the game flips her. Gameplay radius 46. The `death` clip kills the chamber, not the animal: the core burns up white, the brood goes dark, the sac drops to half its held size and the shell's splits open the rest of the way.",
